# --- report-only: wiring either mode would be dishonest -------------------
check-worktree-context.sh: Interactive orientation aid for a HUMAN starting work in the wrong worktree -- it prints which worktree/branch you are in and what that implies. It has no invariant to assert and no failure mode; scripts/new_lane.py only ECHOES its signature and prints "Run `sh scripts/check-worktree-context.sh` before editing", which is advice, not a call. Kept because that advice is load-bearing in a 30-worktree repo, but it is a command a person runs, not a contract. It is NOT a candidate for deletion and NOT a candidate for wiring.
